WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
(fun dance music)

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.720
- I think Japanese pop music will sound

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.680
really fast, really happy.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.270
- Like electronic music
with high-pitched voices.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.850
- It'll probably sound like Katy Perry.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.020
- Like Bjork.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.940
- Da-Ice, sounds like a 90's rap group.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.170
- Whoa, this is fast.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.530
- Oh, it's really happy, it's really fun.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.490
- It's kind of like a Goofy movie.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.200
- I just imagine a bunch of people

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.330
on a dance floor just sweating.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.040
- This is some (bleep)
you could work out to

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.890
and just kill it on the treadmill.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.260
- It definitely sounds like
an American country song.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.720
But like more bells and
(bleep) in the background.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.140
- Beautiful symphony in the background,

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.770
some piano, it's got everything.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.980
It's pulling out all
the stops, for romance.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.600
- This sounds like John Denver.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.810
- He's really sad about it,

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.560
maybe he's asking his dad for a loan.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.530
- This is like you're
coming down on some drugs

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.360
and your ass is done.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.610
- It really sounds a
lot like Sesame Street.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.560
- I could picture myself
crying to this song.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.830
- I'm on a game show, running
down the stairs to this song.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.380
- That is so high-pitched.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.500
- This song feels like it's
a commercial for liquid soap.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.880
- This is exactly like
Rainbow Road on Mario Kart.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.800
- These are like sorority girls,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.970
sitting around talking
(bleep) about someone,

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.180
being real sassy.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.470
- It's probably about friendship,

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.680
it's probably about honesty.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.383
- A 14 year-old girl
that's like trying to get

00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:40.730
out of the house and get away
from her oppressive parents.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.723
And she's like pleading with them,

00:01:42.723 --> 00:01:45.070
but they're like "You're 14
and you sound like a mouse,

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.480
"so we don't trust you."

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.400
- Japanese pop music is delightful.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.947
- It's very upbeat and it's very fast

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.710
and it's very in-your-face.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.250
- It's like you're
inside the circuit board

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.330
of a new computer.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.790
- Every song is like a hug.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:02.750
They're so positive, they're so friendly.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.760
It's like a handshake and
a wink and a milkshake.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.300
It's everything you want in music.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.430
(fun dance music)

